Subject: [PATCH] Honor POPF single-step before a cached successor

POPF has a statically known next RIP. Use the inline successor form so the
existing CheckTF exit path runs before a warm block can execute. A warm CPUID
otherwise leaves the blocked TF bit pending and traps one instruction late.

Source: local macOS Wine queue; see ../../README.md for runtime evidence.
License: ../LICENSE (MIT)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
index 51e263b41629c2141ca35ae3d034170abc2fcb5f..916a56953a39fef19c069066a02a878d49525e32 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
@@ -3776,7 +3776,7 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::POPFOp(OpcodeArgs) {
 
   SetPackedRFLAG(false, Src);
 
-  auto NewRIP = GetRelocatedPC(Op);
+  auto NewRIP = _GetRelocatedPC(Op, 0, true);
   ExitFunction(NewRIP, BranchHint::CheckTF);
   BlockSetRIP = true;
 }
